1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Welcome to the new feature introduction video of Marvelous Designer 2025.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
In the 2025 version, you can experience the latest module library to improve your work efficiency.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,000
In the window options in the main menu, you can choose to display or hide the module library window.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The module editor and module editor in the previous version have been integrated into the module library.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
As in the previous version, click the small arrow in the upper right corner to choose to fold or display the module library window.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
In the previous version, the module components were defined in the module editor.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Then go to the module editor to use it.

8
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Now you can directly define the module components in the module library.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
The module library structure order is the group type style component.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The current structure order is very convenient for the management and integration of these design components.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
If you need to define certain versions of the 3D window as components, you need to follow the structure from the group to find the corresponding style type.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Now we will explain the module library structure from the outside to the inside.

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The outer layer is the group.

14
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
You can choose a group to add styles.

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Or click the add button in the upper right corner to choose the group to add.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Choose the folder to store the group files.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Then the category and style of the subordinates will be stored in this folder.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Click the right arrow on the group file folder.

19
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
You can choose to copy the file folder path or delete the file folder.

20
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
You can click the refresh button to refresh the group list.

21
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
In this tutorial, we will choose the male group.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
When you double click a group,

23
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
it will display the categories below the group.

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
In the upper left corner, you can see the structure of the current folder.

25
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Click the group name to go back to the group list.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
You can use the existing category or click the add button.

27
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Choose to add a category.

28
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Add a clothing category.

29
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Click the refresh button to refresh the category folder.

30
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
However, only the folder that contains the component module will be displayed in the module library.

31
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
In the category folder, click the right arrow.

32
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
You can choose to copy the folder path or delete the file folder.

33
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
In this tutorial, we will choose the Basic Shirts category.

34
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
When you double click the category folder,

35
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
it will display all the categories below the category.

36
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Now, we will add the original half-sleeved T-shirt in the default asset library as an example to define the style.

37
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Click the add button in the upper right corner.

38
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Choose the add style menu.

39
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:47,000
In the pop-up window, enter the name and set the shortcut.

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
The app will default to use the fashion shortcut in the 3D window as the shortcut.

41
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Then click OK.

42
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
If you want to use other pictures as shortcuts,

43
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
you can click the icon on the camera and then go to the folder.

44
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:08,000
You can click the icon mode to switch the display mode to preview or list type.

45
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Click the refresh button to refresh the style list.

46
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Click the right arrow on the style shortcut.

47
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Click the edit style menu.

48
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
You can adjust the style shortcut or name.

49
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:25,000
You can also delete the style type by deleting the options.

50
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Click the add button in the upper right corner.

51
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
You can choose to assign the style to the product line.

52
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
After selecting this option,

53
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
you will add a new product line file to the top of the style under the category.

54
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:41,000
You can expand these styles.

55
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
In the top right corner of the product line list,

56
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
click the add product line option.

57
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,000
In the pop-up window, set the name and shortcut of the new product line.

58
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
You can also choose to add a new product line to the same style,

59
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
and then copy the selected product line.

60
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Add a new product line to it.

61
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
The name and shortcut can also be adjusted.

62
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Double-click to open the product line.

63
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
You can see the style type below.

64
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Now let's select a clothing type first.

65
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Then select a style type.

66
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Here I choose a men's top.

67
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Then select the low-brow embroidery style.

68
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,000
After opening, you can see the component modules of each part under the selected style.

69
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Double-click on other styles.

70
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,000
You can switch to other styles under the same type.

71
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:41,000
You can see the components of the front, back, sleeves, and collar here.

72
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Each type of component has multiple components to change.

73
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
It is the same as the previous modular configuration.

74
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
The double-click module component will be added to the component.

75
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
If there is a component, it will switch to the selected component.

76
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Each part of the clothing is called a component.

77
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:05,000
For example, in T-shirt, the components are the front, back, sleeves, and collar.

78
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
After setting the component type,

79
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
you can define the clothing version in the 3D window

80
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:12,000
and define it as a variety of components.

81
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:19,000
Now let's learn how to add a component type without a component structure.

82
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Click on the Add button in the upper right corner to open the Add menu.

83
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Select Add component type.

84
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:32,000
You can set the new component type in the pop-up window.

85
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,000
The top type is the clothing location of the component.

86
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
The bottom is the type label to set them.

87
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:43,000
In the default situation, the label and the selected component type are the same.

88
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
You can also modify it according to your needs.

89
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
If you want to do different styles or types of design for the same part,

90
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,000
you can use the labels.

91
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Their classification is very useful.

92
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:58,000
You can choose to save the component configuration in the upper right corner.

93
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
After saving the component configuration,

94
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
these component types will be saved as configuration files.

95
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Next time you open it, you can call this component structure.

96
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Select Open component configuration option.

97
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
You can open the previously saved configuration.

98
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Later, we will learn how to use the automatic module fastening label function.

99
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Click on the Add button in the upper right corner to open the new component list.

100
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,000
When all component types are set,

101
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,000
you can start adding components for each type.

102
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Click on the Add new component button in the upper right corner of the component type.

103
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The module generator window will appear.

104
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
In the window pop-up,

105
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
a module type will be displayed in the list.

106
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Here you can manage the components under each type.

107
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:55,000
In the upper right corner, you can choose to edit the module type and configuration.

108
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,000
In the module edit area,

109
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
you can save, edit or delete these module components.

110
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Using the automatic module fastening label option,

111
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:11,000
you can quickly separate the modules into each component type.

112
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
After selecting the option,

113
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
you will see that each module automatically changes its color

114
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
to distinguish its component type.

115
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You can refer to the name and color

116
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
to determine whether these modules are correctly matched to the type of component.

117
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:33,000
If the modules are correctly matched to the component type,

118
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:37,000
click on the save button on the right side of the camera icon.

119
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
You can save the module.

120
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
When the module is correctly saved,

121
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:46,000
the hook icon on the left side will light up,

122
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:49,000
which means that the module has been activated.

123
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
If the automatic module fastening function is not working correctly,

124
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
you can click on the marker icon

125
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
to manually select the module type.

126
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
You can click on the module type

127
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,000
or click on the shift key to select multiple modules.

128
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Then press the enter key to confirm the selection.

129
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
When all the module types are correctly saved,

130
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
the add button on the bottom will activate.

131
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,000
After clicking on the add button,

132
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
a spring will pop up.

133
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Click on the prompt operation

134
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:21,000
to check whether the sewing line structure between the modules is correct.

135
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Click on the sewing line.

136
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:26,000
You will see the marking on the sewing line.

137
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
The prompt is the label of the module component on both sides of the sewing line.

138
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
If the sewing line is wrong,

139
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
please click on the cancel button

140
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
to manually adjust the sewing line

141
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:36,000
and try again.

142
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
After confirming the sewing line,

143
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
click on the confirm key to confirm the definition of the module.

144
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Then adjust the clothing panel

145
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,000
and re-register an additional module.

146
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
Click on the add new module button

147
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
in the upper right corner of the module type.

148
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:57,000
The window of the 2D panel

149
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
will switch to the mode of selecting panels.

150
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Follow the mouse button to select the panels in the window of 2D.

151
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Click on the shift key to select the panels.

152
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Click on the enter key to confirm the selection of panels.

153
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
Then, edit the shrink chart and name.

154
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
As the new modules increase,

155
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
you can switch them in the module library.

156
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
After switching the modules,

157
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
the automatically detect the matching between the modules

158
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
and return the sewing line.

159
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Click on the right button on the module.

160
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
You can select the corresponding option in the menu.

161
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:40,000
Delete the selected module and delete this module.

162
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Share the selected module.

163
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Share the selected module

164
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
to other models under the same category.

165
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Change the shrink chart and replace the shrink chart of the module.

166
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Use the new module to replace it.

167
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Change this module to a newly defined module.

168
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Finally, let's look at the related settings

169
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:09,000
of the module in the user's self-definition.

170
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Go to the main menu.

171
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Set the user's self-definition.

172
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Find other options.

173
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Protect module optimization by limiting editing.

174
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
When this option is selected,

175
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:25,000
add, edit, delete and automatic module optimization labels

176
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
will no longer be usable.

177
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Reduce the number of modules and limit editing.

178
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Prohibit a mixture of modules of different styles.

179
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
After opening the module,

180
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
you can't mix different modules

181
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,000
and make them into one set of clothing.

182
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:46,000
When you add a module from a different style,

183
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:48,000
a warning window will pop up.

184
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
If necessary,

185
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:53,000
you can click the window button and select and verify.

186
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:26,980
Thank you.

